))=0 gives 8x^3+4x^2-4x-1=0 for x=cos(theta). Hence a=1/2, b=-1/2, c=-1/8, and abc=1/32.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2021_AMC_12A_Q22","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"seventh-roots-of-unity","label":"Pair reciprocal seventh roots","methodDirectNodeIds":{"seventh-roots-of-unity":["math:roots-of-unity","math:complex-polar-de-moivre"]},"nodeIds":["math:roots-of-unity","math:complex-polar-de-moivre"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, 1 real pair and 2 nonreal complex pairs","reason":"Set t = x + 1. Then y = t² and ty = 1, so t³ = 1. Its roots are 1 and (-1 ± i√3)/2. The first gives (x,y) = (0,1), while the other two give nonreal pairs.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":["Imaginary pairs in the historical choices means nonreal complex pairs, not pairs of purely imaginary coordinates."],"questionId":"1955_AMC_12_Q43","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_148","cnm_h100"],"id":"substitute-the-repeated-expression","label":"Substitute the repeated expression","methodDirectNodeIds":{"substitute-the-repeated-expression":["math:roots-of-unity","math:sum-difference-cubes","math:completing-square-expression","cnm_h097"]},"nodeIds":["math:roots-of-unity","math:sum-difference-cubes","math:completing-square-expression","cnm_h097","cnm_148","cnm_h100"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 2024","reason":"Add a hypothetical 2016th flight. Each complete 12-flight block has displacement (-6,-12-6√3), so 168 blocks give (-1008,-2016-1008√3). Subtracting flight 2016, whose vector is (1008√3,-1008), leaves (-1008(1+√3),-1008(1+√3)). Its length is 1008√2+1008√6, giving 1008+2+1008+6=2024.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2015_AMC_12B_Q